const REEL_RECIPES=[{"reel":"DecAnkwBLut","title":"Sabudana Khichdi","cat":"Celebrations","excerpt":"Soft sabudana pearls with roasted peanuts and potato — simple, flavourful and made for Navratri fasting.","ingredients":["Sabudana – 1 cup","Water – 1 cup (for soaking)","Peanuts – 1 cup","Boiled potatoes – 2 medium, cubed","Ghee – 1–2 tbsp","Cumin seeds – 1 tsp","Curry leaves – 8–10","Green chillies – 2, chopped","Salt / Sendha namak – to taste","Lemon – ½","Fresh coriander – for garnish"],"steps":["Wash sabudana thoroughly and soak in 1 cup water for 4–6 hours or overnight, until soft. Drain any excess water.","Dry roast peanuts, let them cool, then grind into a coarse powder.","Heat ghee in a pan. Add cumin seeds, curry leaves and green chillies. Sauté for a few seconds.","Add boiled potatoes and fry until slightly golden.","Add soaked sabudana, roasted peanut powder and salt. Mix gently and cook on low-medium heat until the sabudana turns translucent.","Squeeze half a lemon and finish with fresh coriander."],"v":1908,"date":"2026-10-13T15:20:02.000Z"},{"reel":"DeerGDpPg4D","title":"Niramish Cholar Dal","cat":"Bengali & Regional","excerpt":"A no-onion, no-garlic Bengali classic, gently sweet with coconut, cashews and raisins — made for hot luchis.","ingredients":["Chana Dal – 1 cup","Coconut – ¼ cup, chopped into small pieces","Cashews – 10–12","Raisins – 1 tbsp","Ginger – 2 inch","Green chillies – 2","Cumin seeds – 1 tsp","Hing – a pinch","Turmeric powder – ½ tsp","Cumin powder – ½ tsp","Coriander powder – ½ tsp","Sugar – to taste","Ghee – 1 tsp","Garam masala – ½ tsp","Salt – to taste"],"steps":["Wash and boil chana dal until soft but not mushy.","Make a paste of ginger +green chillies; add turmeric, cumin powder, coriander powder, and a little water.","Heat mustard oil / Ghee in a pan. Add cumin seeds, hing, and chopped coconut. Fry until the coconut turns light golden.","Add the prepared masala paste and sauté until fragrant.","Add boiled chana dal along with some cooking water. Mix well and simmer for a few minutes.","Add chopped cashews, raisins, and sugar. Adjust salt and cook until the dal reaches your preferred consistency.","Finish with ghee and garam masala."],"v":2531,"date":"2026-10-14T15:14:27.000Z"},{"reel":"DdjdadYTNvT","title":"Air-Fried Chicken Kebabs","cat":"Everyday Cooking","excerpt":"Crispy outside, juicy inside and packed with protein — cheesy kebabs made with minimal oil.","ingredients":["500g chicken","4 tbsp thick curd (hung curd works best)","1 tsp ginger paste","1 tsp garlic paste","2 tsp black pepper","1 tsp garam masala (I used homemade — check out my profile for the recipe!)","Salt to taste","2 cubes processed cheese, grated","A little ghee for brushing"],"steps":["Mix everything together and marinate for at least 1 hour. The longer you marinate, the juicier and more flavourful the chicken gets!","Brush the air fryer basket with a little ghee and arrange the chicken in a single layer.","Air fry at 180°C for 20 minutes, flipping halfway through. Increase to 190°C for the last 5 minutes for that beautiful golden colour."],"v":246446,"date":"2026-09-21T15:15:08.000Z"},{"reel":"DdEj0avTzi4","title":"One-Pot Mushroom Biryani","cat":"Quick & Easy","excerpt":"Mushrooms marinated in curd and biryani masala, cooked with the rice in a single pot — cooker or kadai.","ingredients":["Button mushrooms – 400 g, halved","Thick curd – ½ cup","Turmeric – ¼ tsp","Cumin powder – 1 tsp","Coriander powder – 1 tsp","Kashmiri chilli powder – 1 tsp","Basmati/Jeera rice – 1½ cups, washed and soaked for 20 minutes *(if you have time)"],"steps":["Heat some ghee and oil in a pressure cooker or heavy kadai. Add cardamom, cloves, cinnamon and black pepper and let them become aromatic.","Add sliced onions and fry until translucent. Add 1 tbsp each ginger and garlic paste and cook until the raw smell disappears.","Add the marinated mushrooms along with the marinade. Cook on medium-high heat for 5–7 minutes. The mushrooms will release water, so continue cooking until the masala reduces and thickens slightly.","Add the soaked and drained basmati/jeera rice and gently mix everything together.","For the water, I generally follow a 1 cup rice : 2 cups water ratio. However, mushrooms release a lot of water, so check how much liquid is already present in the masala and reduce the added water accordingly.Add salt if needed.","Pressure cooker: Close the lid and cook for 3–4 whistles on high heat. Switch off and allow the pressure to release naturally before opening.","Kadai/pot: Cover tightly and cook on low-medium heat for 12–15 minutes. Switch off and let it rest covered for another 10 minutes.","Gently fluff the rice and serve hot with raita and salad."],"v":39278,"date":"2026-09-09T15:15:05.000Z"},{"reel":"DeKFYa7ExFc","title":"Kolkata Bhetki Fish Fry","cat":"Bengali & Regional","excerpt":"Proper Kolkata cabin-style fish fry: a herby green marinade, a crunchy crumb crust, kasundi on the side.","ingredients":["Bhetki fillet – 500g","Onion – 1 medium","Coriander leaves – 1 big handful","Green chillies – 2-3","Garlic – 5–6 cloves","Ginger – 2-inch","Bengali garam masala – ½ tsp","Black pepper –1 tsp","Msg- ¼ tsp","Sugar – ½ tsp","Salt – to taste","Lime juice – 1 tsp","Maida – as required","Breadcrumbs – as required","Egg wash – as required","Oil – for frying"],"steps":["Pat the fish completely dry. Blend the marinade ingredients into a smooth paste, coat the fish and refrigerate for 20–30 minutes.","Coat each fillet in maida → dip in the egg → breadcrumbs for that signature crunchy crust.","Shape neatly and fry in hot oil on medium-high heat until beautifully golden and crisp."],"v":2720,"date":"2026-10-06T15:15:01.000Z"},{"reel":"DeW8X2uzaLH","title":"Navratri Thali","cat":"Baking & Desserts","excerpt":"A vrat-friendly thali of dry kala chana and rich sooji halwa, served with hot pooris.","ingredients":["Kala chana – 250g (1½ cups)","Water – 3–4 cups","Bay leaf – 1","Salt – to taste ( rock salt for vrat)","Kashmiri chilli powder – 1 tsp","Turmeric – ¼ tsp","Coriander powder – 2 tsp","Kala namak – ½ tsp","Ghee","Jeera – ½ tsp","Hing – ¼ tsp"],"steps":["Soak kala chana overnight. Pressure cook with water, bay leaf, and salt until tender (approx. 4–6 whistles).","Mix all the masala ingredients with ⅓ cup water.","Heat ghee, add jeera, hing and ginger. Sauté briefly.","Add the masala mixture and cook for 3–4 minutes.","Add boiled chana paste , and some reserved chana water. Cook until the masala thickens , then add boiled chana and saute until coats the chana.","Finish with roasted and ground jeera +ajwain , amchur, ginger juliennes and coriander, sooji Halwa Recipe","Rich, aromatic and melt-in-the-mouth Sooji Halwa, made with lots of ghee and crunchy dry fruits!, sooji / Semolina – ½ cup, ghee – ½ cup","Sugar – ⅓ cup (adjust to taste)","Water – 1½ cups (adjust consistency)","Cashews, almonds & raisins – ¼ cup","Heat a little ghee in a pan, fry the dry fruits until golden, chop and keep aside.","In the same pan, add the remaining ghee and sooji. Roast on low-medium flame until golden brown and aromatic.","Gradually add hot water while stirring continuously to avoid lumps.","Once the sooji absorbs the water, add sugar and mix well."],"v":4252,"date":"2026-10-11T15:16:48.000Z"},{"reel":"Dc_YK4Xznw8","title":"Homemade Biryani Masala","cat":"Everyday Cooking","excerpt":"Whole spices roasted gently and ground at home — the fragrant base for every biryani she makes.","ingredients":["Green Cardamom – 16pcs (4 g)","Black Cardamom – 2 pcs (1.5 g)","Cinnamon – 4-inch total (2 g)","Cloves – 16 pcs / 1½ tsp (3 g)","Mace/Javitri – 1 flower","Nutmeg/Jaiphal – ½ nutmeg (2.5 g)","Shah Jeera – 2 tsp (4 g)","Jeera/Cumin Seeds – 2 tsp (4 g)","Coriander Seeds/Dhaniya – 1 tbsp","Star Anise – 1 medium","Kabab Chini – 2 tsp ( i forgot to add)","Black Peppercorns – 2 tsp (5 g)","White Peppercorns – 1 tsp (2.5–3 g)","Rose petals - 1 tsp ( i forgot to add)"],"steps":["Dry roast all the spices except jeera and shah jeera on low heat for 2–3 minutes, just until aromatic. Don’t let the spices brown. Add jeera and shah jeera last .","Switch off the heat,and toss them in the residual heat.","Let everything cool completely, then grind into a fine powder.","Store in a clean, dry, airtight glass jar."],"v":2096,"date":"2026-09-07T15:04:42.000Z"},{"reel":"DblRnP4zmwt","title":"Andhra Green Chilli Chicken","cat":"Everyday Cooking","excerpt":"Chicken in a fiery green paste of chillies, mint and curry leaves, finished with tamarind and black pepper.","ingredients":["Boneless chicken: 500g","Onion: 1 medium, roughly chopped","Fresh green chillies: 3- 4( depends on your spice level)","Ginger: 1-inch piece","Garlic: 5–6 cloves","Fresh mint leaves: ½ cup","Curry leaves: 15–20","Turmeric: ½ tsp","Cinnamon: 1 small piece","Cloves: 3","Fennel seeds: 1 tsp","Salt: 1 tsp","Water: 1–2 tbsp, only if needed for grinding","Oil ( i used Rice bran oil )","Green chillies: 2, cut into pieces","Concentrated tamarind water: 1 tbsp","Freshly crushed black pepper: ½ tsp","Fresh curry leaves: 8–10","Optional cornflour slurry","Cornflour: 1 tsp","Water: 2 tbsp"],"steps":["Blend the onion, green chillies, ginger, garlic, mint, curry leaves, turmeric, cinnamon, cloves and fennel seeds into a smooth paste. Add only a little water if required.","Mix the paste with the chicken and salt. Marinate for at least 30 minutes if you have time","Heat the oil in a pan. Add the marinated chicken and cook on medium-high heat for 5–6 minutes, stirring regularly.","Cover and cook , chicken will first release water. Continue cooking until the moisture reduces and the masala starts coating the chicken.","Add the extra green chillies and tamarind water. Cook for another 3–4 minutes.","For a thicker, glossy coating, add the cornflour slurry and cook for 30–60 seconds.","Finish with freshly crushed black pepper and fresh curry leaves."],"v":35007,"date":"2026-08-03T15:14:38.000Z"},{"reel":"Da8EK4hTBUr","title":"Chicken Maharani","cat":"Everyday Cooking","excerpt":"A rich chicken curry built on curd-marinated chicken and freshly roasted whole spices.","ingredients":["Boneless chicken: 500g (Chicken thigh is juicier, breast is leaner.)","Curd: ½ cup","Ginger-garlic paste: 2tsp","Salt: to taste","Black pepper powder: ½ tsp","Lemon juice: 1 tsp","Onion: 2 medium, sliced","Cashews: 10–12 pieces","Green chilli: 1–2","Water: as needed for blending","½ tsp coriander seeds","½ tsp cumin seeds","½ tsp fennel seeds","¼ tsp nutmeg","1 small piece of mace","5 green cardamom","½ tsp black pepper","½ tsp clove","A small piece of cinnamon"],"steps":["In a bowl, add chicken, curd, ginger-garlic paste, salt, black pepper, and lemon juice.","Mix well and rest for 30 minutes.","Dry roast all the whole spices over low heat until aromatic, then grind it.","In a pan, add 1 tsp oil and sliced onions, cashews, and green chilli with a little water.","Cover and cook for 5–6 minutes, until the onions turn soft.","Cool it and blend into a smooth paste.(This gives the creamy Maharani-style gravy without using too much cream.","Heat 1 tbsp oil or ghee in a pan. Add the marinated chicken and cook on medium flame for 5–6 minutes.","Add the onion-cashew paste , spice mix, and mix well.","Cover and cook for 8–10 minutes, until the chicken is fully cooked.","Add kasuri methi, fresh cream, and a tiny pinch of sugar if needed.","Mix and cook for only 1 minute on low flame.","Your Chicken Maharani is ready."],"v":3851,"date":"2026-07-18T15:10:59.000Z"},{"reel":"DYznkqgTTOa","title":"Husband's Lunch Box","cat":"Everyday Cooking","excerpt":"A wholesome office lunch box built around a fresh coriander chutney.","ingredients":["2 cups fresh coriander leaves","3 garlic cloves","2 green chillies","1/2 lemon","1/2 tsp salt","1/2 tsp sugar","2–3 tbsp water"],"steps":["Add coriander, garlic, green chillies, salt, sugar, and lemon juice to a mixer jar.","Add little water and blend into a smooth chutney.","Taste and adjust salt or lemon as needed.","Mix it with curd and use as a dip or directly use the chutney for sandwich , fries etc."],"v":3350,"date":"2026-05-26T15:15:14.000Z"},{"reel":"DY4wvmaT5k3","title":"Kung Pao Chicken","cat":"Global Flavours","excerpt":"Crisp chicken thighs tossed with dried red chillies, garlic and ginger in a glossy sauce.","ingredients":["500 g boneless chicken thighs","salt to taste","1 tsp black pepper","2 tbsp cornflour","1 egg","6 tbsp oil","1 tbsp chopped garlic","1 tbsp julienne ginger","1 medium onion (cubed)","1/4 cup roasted peanuts","4–5 dried red chillies","3 tbsp soy sauce","2 tbsp oyster sauce","2 tbsp red chilli sauce","1 tbsp cornflour mixed with 1/2 cup water"],"steps":["Marinate chicken with salt, pepper, egg, and 2 tbsp cornflour for 15–20 mins.","Add 4 tbsp oil and Fry the chicken until 2-3 mins max, add 2 tbsp oil","Add red chilli ,garlic and ginger, sauté for 30 seconds.","Add onion and bell papers , Stir fry for 2-3 minutes, then add the sauce.","Add fried chicken,peanuts , cornflour slurry and salt to taste","Mix well on high flame until the sauce thickens and coats the chicken. ADD SOME SPRING ONION AS WELL ( I forgot)","Serve hot, nutrition (Approx.), total recipe, calories: ~1750–1850 kcal, protein: ~95–100 g","Per serving (divided into 4), calories: ~440–460 kcal, protein: ~24–25 g"],"v":3402,"date":"2026-05-28T15:25:07.000Z"},{"reel":"DYmvrECz93U","title":"Chicken Chukauni","cat":"Global Flavours","excerpt":"Pan-fried chicken folded into spiced curd with a mustard-oil tadka — a high-protein side dish.","ingredients":["Chicken breast: 500g","Salt: to taste","Turmeric: ½ tsp","Kashmiri red chilli powder: 1 tsp","Black pepper: ½ tsp","Oil for frying: 1 tbsp or as needed","Curd: 250g","Salt: to taste","Monk fruit sweetener: as per taste /or you can use normal sugar","Mustard oil","Turmeric: ¼ tsp","Kashmiri red chilli powder: ½ tsp","Kasuri methi: 1 tsp"],"steps":["Take 500g chicken breast in a bowl.","Add salt, turmeric, Kashmiri red chilli powder, and black pepper. Mix well and marinate for 10mins.","Heat a pan and add a little oil.","Add the marinated chicken pieces and pan-fry until golden from outside and fully cooked inside. Keep it aside.","In a separate bowl, take 250g curd.","Add salt and monk fruit sweetener. Beat well until smooth and creamy.","Now prepare the tadka. Heat mustard oil in a small pan.","Add turmeric, Kashmiri red chilli powder, and kasuri methi.","Pour this hot tadka over the beaten curd and mix well.","Take the cooked chicken , add onion , green chilli and coriander and add the curd mixture into it. Mix gently.Serve as a high-protein side dish."],"v":6500,"date":"2026-05-21T15:15:11.000Z"},{"reel":"DYfCyX8zzds","title":"Quick Chicken Rice","cat":"Quick & Easy","excerpt":"Her most-watched reel: one-pot pressure-cooker chicken rice, on the table in about 15 minutes.","ingredients":["Chicken – 500g","Curd – ½ cup","Ginger and garlic paste – 1 tbsp each","Biryani masala – 1.5–2 tbsp","Salt to taste","Oil – 4 tbsp","Onion – 2 big, thinly sliced","Rice – 2 cups, soaked","Water – approx. 3 cups"],"steps":["Marinate chicken with curd, ginger garlic paste, biryani masala and salt.","Heat oil in a pressure cooker. Add sliced onions and fry till golden brown.","Add marinated chicken and cook till the raw smell goes away.","Add soaked rice and mix gently.","Add water. Normally 1 cup rice needs 2 cups water, but because curd and chicken release water, add 1 cup less than usual.","Pressure cook on high flame for 4 whistles.","Let it rest closed for 5 minutes.","Open, fluff gently and serve hot."],"v":482687,"date":"2026-05-18T15:31:14.000Z"},{"reel":"DX9i3KpT4a1","title":"Paneer Puffs","cat":"Baking & Desserts","excerpt":"Caramelised onion and paneer filling wrapped in flaky puff pastry — an easy tea-time and tiffin snack.","ingredients":["Paneer","Onion – 2 medium, thinly sliced","Capsicum – 1, sliced","Garlic – 1 tbsp, chopped","Ginger – 1 tbsp, chopped","Green chilli – optional","Salt – as needed","Black pepper – as needed","Sugar – a little","Oil – as needed","Egg wash or milk wash","Sauce mix","Soy sauce – 2 tbsp","Green chilli sauce – 2 tbsp","Vinegar – 2 tsp"],"steps":["Heat some oil in a pan.","Add thinly sliced onions and cook until fully brown ( caramelized)","Add chopped garlic and ginger. Sauté for a few seconds","Add capsicum and green chilli. Stir-fry for 2–3 minutes.","Add paneer and mix gently.","Add soy sauce, green chilli sauce, and vinegar.","Add salt, black pepper, and a little sugar.","Cook for 2–3 minutes by adding little water and cook until the filling becomes dry.","Let the paneer filling cool completely.","Take puff pastry sheets or patties dough and add the paneer filling inside.","Seal the edges properly.","Brush the top with egg wash or milk wash.","Bake in a preheated oven at 180–200°C until golden and crispy.","Your paneer patties are ready."],"v":3242,"date":"2026-05-05T15:15:02.000Z"},{"reel":"DWjAyAaz5BK","title":"Palakura Pappu","cat":"Everyday Cooking","excerpt":"Andhra-style toor dal cooked with spinach — simple, comforting and best with steamed rice and ghee.","ingredients":["1 cup toor dal (arhar dal)","2 cups palak (spinach), washed & chopped","1 medium onion (chopped)","1 medium tomato (chopped)","3–4 garlic cloves (crushed or sliced)","½ tsp turmeric powder","½ tsp Red chilli powder","Salt to taste","Tamarind juice","Water as needed","1–2 tbsp oil or ghee","1 tsp mustard seeds","1 tsp cumin seeds","2 dried red chilies","8–10 curry leaves","A pinch of hing (asafoetida)"],"steps":["Cook the dal","Wash toor dal and pressure cook with enough water for 3–4 whistles until soft . Mash lightly and keep aside, prepare tadka","Heat oil/ghee, add mustard seeds, cumin seeds, dried red chilies, curry leaves, and hing . Let it splutter and turn aromatic.","Add chopped onion, garlic ,tomato, crushed garlic and spinach . Cook with a little water until everything softens, combine","Add the cooked dal to the spinach mixture.","Add salt, tamarind juice and let it simmer for 5–7 minutes for flavors to blend.","Serve hot with steamed rice and a drizzle of ghee for ultimate comfort!"],"v":3772,"date":"2026-03-31T10:53:12.000Z"}];
